All 37 targeted mixed-font controls, 100 varied mixed-font sequences and
100 retained single-font sequences match compared Java fragment records,
row geometry and extents bit for bit. Selected independent native
fixtures retain regressions for font boundaries, aliases, unavailable
slots, whitespace heights and empty final rows.

The packaged-engine fallback regression connects authored disjoint
coverage and per-face metrics to actual line construction. Original
Renoir scaling at 0x180068a70 and cohtml metric conversion establish
14-pixel line advance for that 13-pixel fixture, including native float
rounding before the ceiling. CSS policy selection, complex-script/bidi
layout, fitting and complete mixed-font screen rendering remain open.

Resolve regular gameplay font families in the original locale-dependent
order before ordinary per-scalar assignment. Keep the caller's primary
family first and preserve unavailable slots. The ordered CJK and Arabic
families and the Mongolian/Syriac/Tamil tail are not interchangeable.
The API accepts native-case locale identifiers and resolves only the
registered 400-weight normal faces used by this gameplay path.
It does not infer a locale from a text's characters.

Execute the unchanged locale-selection function and family constants in
shipped 1.26.60.5 gameplay-6de8e340eddced55490b.js, SHA-256
9e7efe423b6cc8a1c1fa92756bd181675cffa51a4728bce386b0081cad1bb979.
Its CSS variable supplies the fallback list after the selected primary
family. Japanese and Korean use prefix checks, Chinese variants use exact
native identifiers, and Arabic requires the native ar_ prefix.

Original target FreeType face parsing and character maps establish glyph
indices for a/CJK/b in Minecraft Seven and six Noto families. The ordinary
cohtml constructor then executes assignment with those coverage results
and explicitly supplied advance/metric interfaces. Thirteen locale and
unavailable-primary controls match the packaged engine's real family
order, glyph indices and selected slots, while preserving primary Latin.
The unused tail interfaces do not establish their font coverage. Complete
CSS cascade, weight/style substitution, complex-script/bidi dispatch,
consumer policy selection and rendered locale parity remain open.

Apply the collapsed trailing-whitespace reserve to row widths before
alignment, rather than adding it to a visible glyph or fragment advance.
Each row admits the reserve only up to its available width, with the
first row's indent considered separately. Existing overflow is retained.
Keep negative reserves and the native 0.001 tolerance. The old layout
entry points retain their zero-reserve behavior.

Original target cohtml 0x18003c4cc executes between original construction,
alignment and extent queries in 26 native controls. They establish full,
partial and rejected reserves, indents, negative widths, the exact
floating tolerance, empty input and mixed-font fragment preservation.
The shared regression compares row and fragment geometry with that
independent output. Full measurement-cache and fitting policy selection
remain outside this port.

Convert host pointer input independently from native drawing scale.
Java26.3 GuiRenderer projects framebuffer dimensions divided by the
integer GUI scale, but MouseHandler uses ceiling-sized GUI width and
height. Retain each actual input axis factor in NativeUiViewport and
apply it consistently to clicks, release, movement, drag deltas and
scroll positions. Read the current unrounded pointer before native
render extraction. Native GuiData layout and physical drawing remain
unchanged. Explicit four-argument viewports retain uniform input units.

A real authored-screen action regression routes MouseHandler coordinates
through the production adapter. The old conversion moves an inside point
past a button edge on each rounded axis, including a HiDPI host. Remove
the old test that treated input as the inverse of rendering; that equality
is false at ceiling-sized host dimensions. Existing versioned native
viewport-scale controls retain their separate layout contract. This fixes
host input ownership, not complete native screen/device parity.

BREAKING CHANGE: Replace NativeUiViewport.pointer with pointerX or
pointerY. Host input conversion is axis-specific.

Retain the native View hold countdown separately from controller gesture time.
Controller result bits start a binary32 0.3-second frame countdown, stop it,
or suppress both updates. Expiry is strictly negative; event data retain the
starting pointer and a strict five-unit displacement gate on each axis.
Original Bedrock 1.26.60.5 countdown and result-composition controls establish
these boundaries. Feature controllers own admission and completion.

Cull native draws after window clipping when either pixel dimension is
zero. Preserve empty fractional clips during GUI-coordinate conversion.
Enchanted protocol 2225 hub return can leave a clipped 835-by-zero draw;
passing it to the render backend crashes. Disabling its scissor would
leak pixels, so skip that draw while preserving the other draw commands.

Receive chat-item HUD scenes on a separately advertised capability. Reuse
the existing layout, resource ownership and animation lifecycle, while
keeping expired creation identities until the next bounded refresh. A
new notification must not restart an older notification's clock or revive
controls already destroyed by their authored animations. Disconnect and
explicit clear still release the retained scene.
